  "prefLabel": "Env-A 3203.25 Excess emissions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 3203.25 “Excess emissions” means emissions of nitrogen oxides reported by a budget source during the control period, rounded to the nearest whole ton, which are greater than the equivalent number of allowances allocated to, or which are available in, the budget source NOx allowance tracking system compliance or overdraft account by the allowance transfer deadline for that season.\n\nSource. #11001, eff 1-1-16; ss by #14632, eff 6-25-26, EXPIRES: 6-25-36 (formerly Env-A 3203.26)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a3200.html"
}
